 "doc": "The same Earth-like ascent with float64 directions: float64 gaussians, the per-vortex terms cast to float32 and accumulated in float32, so the sum still rounds per vortex. Tolerance rtol 1e-5, atol 1e-6 (the default): the output is float32, so a float64 nudge of the inputs changes nothing (0 observed) and the other float64 order (reversed vortices, one cast at the end of an all-float64 accumulation) differs by at most 2.4e-7 (0.03 of the band). Conventions of cloudgen.sphere read here: lonlat_to_dir(lon, lat) = (cos lat cos lon, cos lat sin lon, sin lat) with float64 numpy cos and sin (right-handed, z north, longitude grows east; a vortex center is that direction); normalize(v) = v / |v| (plain division, no epsilon: a zero vector gives NaN).",
